Variables: 

Comment in TS: 

Use of Comment:
To explain the code
To stop executing certain portion of the code

Single line comment --> //
Multiline comment   --> /* .......... */ 

data types in TypeScript

number --> non-decimal & decimal 
string --> store multiple characters
Boolean--> true/false
any    --> any value
Enum   --> store sequence of constant values 

Steps to run your typescript code

trans compile your typescript code into javascript file(ensure to save) --> tsc nameOfTheFile.ts
2. create a html file       
<html>
<script src= "nameOfTheFile.ts">
</script>
</html>
3. Go to the folder where we created these files 
4. Open the browser file
5. Right click on the browser --> Select inspect option
6. Go to console tab ---Result or output is displayed

We have two options for storing <value>
1. Variables
2. Array
-> when we have to store single value, we prefer Variables
-> when we have to sore multiple values of similar data type, we prefer array

===========================Operators===================================

==========================Flow control statements and loops===================

Selection| Iterative | Transfer
if-else  |  while    | break
switch   |   for     | continue 


if-else

if(condition)
{
    code here will execute only if the condition is true;
}
else
{
    code here will execute only if condition is false;
}

// Multiple if else if else 

if(condition1)
{
    code here will execute only if the condition is true;
}

else if(condition2)
{
    code here will execute only if the condition2 is true;
}

else if(condition3)
{
    code here will execute only if the condition3 is true;
}
.....
.....
.....
.....

else if(conditionN)
{
    code here will execute only if the conditionN is true;
}

else
{
    code here will execute if none of the above condition/s are true;
}


====================== Class and Objects =================================   

A class is a Template
Every copy of the class is known as its object 

Object Structure:

var product = {
    id: 12345,
    name: "Iphone",
    color: "White"
}


Students: fName, lName, gender, age
Object :   Students stud= new Students();
stud.fname;
stud.lName;




statements: to make decisions
loops: while, for loop, advanced for loop[for each, for in ]

for(var x :arrayName) //Jason, Roger, Wael, Jay, Kerrie, Rose 
{
    system.out.println(x);
}

==========================Loops============================================

//Loops
  //while loop
  //for loop
  //for in loop

  variable;
  while(condition)
  {
      this part of code will execute only if condition is true;
      Increment/Decrement operator;
  }


  for(variable;condition;Increment/Decrement operator)
  {
      this part of code will execute only if condition is true;
  }


  //for loop --> When we know the end of the loop 
  //while loop ---> not sure when the end will be reached 

  //12,34,5,6,8,32,54